{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Operators and If\u2026 Else\u2026Else if"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are discussing about PHP. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about common solutions to problems in spoken or written documents.  Talk about programming and data base related to hypertext preprocessor in spoken or written documents. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Must Have, May Have, Might Have"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Must have</b>, <b>may have</b>, and <b>might have</b> are modal perfects. They help us to speculate about the past or present; in other words, they express probability in the past or present. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the expressions <b>may have</b> and <b>might have</b> to show that a situation could possibly take place in the present or past. In fact, it does not imply a high level of certitude. Now, what is the difference between them? Remember that both, may and might, express possibility and are, in the majority of cases, switchable. However, some contexts can make us use one expression over the other. For example, if we don't know about the level of certainty of the situation being referred, both expressions are useful. However, if the situation being referred didn't take place at all, it is best to use the expression <b>might have</b>. </br></br>Now, the structure that we use is the following: </br></br><center>Subject + may have + action verb in past participle form + complement.</br></br>Subject + might have + action verb in past participle form + complement.</center></br>For example:</br><i>As of now, <b>you might have become</b> an expert in PHP. </i> (We speculate about the present.)</br><i><b>An exam might have been</b> a terrible idea for last class as nobody knew about the topic. </i>  (We make reference to a past event that didn't take place.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, the expression <b>must have</b> implies a high level of certitude; in other words, you are sure about something. The structure that we use is basically the same as in the other two expressions: </br></br><center>Subject + must have + action verb in past participle form + complement.</center></br>For example:</br><i><b>She must have passed</b> the exam, she studied very hard for it. </br>As of now, <b>the teacher must have graded</b> the exams."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Wow, I must have contacted you before."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It might have been a great idea."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Need and Causative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <b>need + causative</b> when we need another person to do something for us. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the <b>need + causative</b> whenever we want to mention that an action was done for us by another person. Apart from this, we can we use two different verbs to introduce the causative, which can be either <b>get</b> or <b>have</b>. The structure that we use is the following: </br></br><center>Person who needed the action + need(s) + to get / to have + object + action verb in past participle + complement (or doer). </center></br>For example:</br><i><b>We need to have this exam presented</b> by the students next Monday.</br><b>  I need to get this topic explained </b> by somebody next class. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to have that topic explained by anybody as soon as possible.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "For example, if we need to have some arrays compared, we will have to use PHP array operators."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "List of Programming and Computer Science Terms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are some <b>important terms</b> related to the field of computer science that we have to check.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some specialized terms that we, as future programmers or workers in the field of computing, have to be familiar with. Check the following chart to learn about some of them: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>TERM\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>DESCRIPTION\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>Unreachable Code\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An unreachable code refers to a source code that is not executable because there is a lack of a control flow path that the system can take towards the code.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>Upgrade\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The action in which a product or service is updated to the last technology available, being able to have a better and improved service or piece of hardware. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>User Interface\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The user interface refers to the elements that are designed so the user can interact, through them, with the system, application or website.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b><center>Utility Computing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A strategy that maximizes the efficient use of resources and minimize costs as the computer resources and infrastructure management are given to the customer just as they are needed. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hard luck "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to express sympathy towards someone who has failed at doing something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Hard luck! What did they ask you about?  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "have no clue "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not to know anything about something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I had to name different kinds of operators, but I had no clue about them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "carry out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to execute a process or an action"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ones that I use the most are arithmetic operators, which we use to carry out operations of addition, subtraction and multiplication."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "execute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to run something on a system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It's a conditional statement, which means that if the condition presented in the statement is affirmative, a specific code will be executed."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "array "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the total amount of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, if we need to have some arrays compared, we will have to use PHP array operators."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Jackie</b>: Hi, John! How was your exam? </br>\n<b>John</b>: I couldn't pass it. If I had studied everything about operators in PHP and if/else statements, I wouldn't have failed it.  </br>\n<b>Jackie</b>: Hard luck! What did they ask you about? </br>\n<b>John</b>: I had to name different kinds of operators, but I had no clue about them. I need to have that topic explained by anybody as soon as possible.  </br>\n<b>Jackie</b>: I can help! If you want to understand what operators are, you have to know that we use them to perform operations on variables and values. As you know, there are different kinds of operators in PHP, such as logical, assignment, arithmetic, comparison, increment/decrement operators, array, among others. The ones that I use the most are arithmetic operators, which we use to carry out operations of addition, subtraction and multiplication. We also, combine conditional statements using the logical operators.  </br>"}, {"time": "70000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>John</b>: Wow, I must have contacted you before. What about the if/else statement?</br>\n<b>Jackie</b>: It's a conditional statement, which means that if the condition presented in the statement is affirmative, a specific code will be executed. In fact, different actions will be performed if the condition is met or affirmative. On the contrary, another code or action will be performed if the condition is negative. </br>"}, {"time": "102000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>John</b>: Thank you, Jackie. It's clearer now. I must have asked you about all of this before my exam. </br>\n<b>Jackie</b>:  It might have been a great idea. Now, I'm sure that if your teacher gives you a second chance, you'll improve your grade. However, don't forget to check the topic related to the operators. For example, if we need to have some arrays compared, we will have to use PHP array operators. On the other hand, is we need to increment or decrease the value of a variable, we will have to use the corresponding increment or decrement operator. </br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n8le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n8le01ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n8le01ob11re5vid01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [{"type": "template_override", "content": 2}], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list and describe some operators in PHP."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain if\u2026 Else\u2026Elseif statements in PHP."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can compare some operators in PHP."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What is the relationship between a webpage and PHP? Share your thoughts. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are some of the most common PHP functions people use? List as many as you can remember. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"